  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At a Northern Plains Zombie Alliance meeting, Yin Liu Gong names a mission tied to Red Fiend Divine Boat. Fang Yuan recalls the house as a glorious flying boat that charged freely across the battlefield in the five regions chaotic war. Gu Ye calls it a famous Immortal Gu House and says a Northern Plains lone cultivator obtained the entire recipe, could not refine it, and tried selling it everywhere; the alliance leader paid a huge price for about half of that recipe. Yin Liu Gong adds that the seller broke the deal and now wants to sell the boat recipe and the core Immortal Gu recipe at auction. Fang Yuan does not favor Zombie Alliance’s chances, because in his previous life the force that controlled Red Fiend Divine Boat was not them.",
      "chapters": [
        741
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "fac_zombie_alliance",
        "char_yin_liu_gong",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_gu_ye",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "sys_gu_recipe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The seller is only rank six and has no backing. Zombie Alliance already holds most of the recipe and still needs the remaining core Immortal Gu recipes and the secret methods for coordinating the Gu worms. The branch sends a rank seven immortal zombie and two rank six immortal zombies to hunt the seller for both reputation and the complete recipe.",
      "chapters": [
        742
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Deviation (recorded): this page is filed under gu-houses because Red Fiend Divine Boat is a named Immortal Gu House. The chapters in scope mainly track its recipe and sale, not a fixed map seat.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Near the end of Qin Bai Sheng’s auction, the complete Gu recipe for Red Fiend Divine Boat and the method to use it go up for sale, with the seller asking for wood path cultivation aid. Zombie Alliance fails to strike the hidden lone cultivator and cannot stop the listing; Yin Liu Gong and Dragon Commander Ye Cha are forced into the bidding as super forces and rank eight experts join. Meng tribe and Yuan tribe both offer wood path Immortal Gu among other stakes.",
      "chapters": [
        762
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "recipe-auction",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_qin_bai_sheng",
        "char_dragon_commander_ye_cha",
        "fac_meng_tribe",
        "fac_yuan_tribe",
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The recipe draws only rank seven Gu Immortals from super forces or rank eight experts into real competition. No core Immortal Gu are sold with it; even a winning bid still leaves a huge refinement cost ahead. Through a three-party deal, Heavenly Lord Bai Zu wins the complete recipe while Fang Yuan obtains unravel mystery Immortal Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        763
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "recipe-auction",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_heavenly_lord_bai_zu",
        "gu_unravel_mystery"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After the auction, Yao Huang tries to buy the recipe from Heavenly Lord Bai Zu and is refused; Bai Zu says he plans to found a tribe and will not sell such a treasure lightly.",
      "chapters": [
        764
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "recipe-auction",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_yao_huang",
        "fac_bai_zu_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan later lists Red Fiend Divine Boat with other Immortal Gu Houses as a war fortress style asset, the same class as Eighty-Eight True Yang Building, Water Pavilion, Heaven Overseeing Tower, and Profound Ice House.",
      "chapters": [
        837
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
